{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Topology.FractalCantorFockWitness\n\nReal Cantor-boundary Clifford/Fock witness packet.\n\nOwner lane:\n\n`Erlangen/binary boundary -> Cantor addresses -> tilt/switch operators ->\nreal doubled Hestenes/Krein Clifford representation -> Fock/CAR witness`.\n\nThe tilt/switch operators are not identified with repository light-cone arrows\nor Tomita mirror data by definition.  Those identifications are explicit\ncalibration fields.\n\nThe metric graph embedding paper belongs to the finite metric graph-compression\nlane, not to this Clifford/Fock witness lane.\n-/\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Topology.FractalCantorFockWitness\n\n/-- Symbolic Cantor boundary: infinite binary address space. -/\nabbrev CantorBoundary := ℕ → Bool\n\n/-- Finite Cantor address of depth `n`. -/\nabbrev CantorAddress (n : ℕ) := Fin n → Bool\n\n/-- Finite real/doubled function space over the depth-`n` Cantor endpoint set. -/\nabbrev FiniteCantorFunctionSpace (n : ℕ) (Value : Type*) :=\n  CantorAddress n → Value\n\n/-- Infinite real/doubled Cantor function-space packet, standing for the `L²(K)` socket. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure RealDoubledCantorFunctionSpace where\n  Space : Type*\n  MeasureData : Type*\n  RealHilbertWitness : Type*\n  DoubledKreinWitness : Type*\n\n/--\nTilt/switch operator system.\n\n`T p` is the tilt operator and `S p` is the switch operator.  The owner relation\nis local anticommutation at the same address slot and commutation at distinct\nslots.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure TiltSwitchSystem\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  T : ℕ → Op\n  S : ℕ → Op\n\n  T_sq :\n    ∀ p, T p * T p = 1\n\n  S_sq :\n    ∀ p, S p * S p = 1\n\n  T_comm :\n    ∀ p q, T p * T q = T q * T p\n\n  S_comm :\n    ∀ p q, S p * S q = S q * S p\n\n  T_S_comm_ne :\n    ∀ p q, p ≠ q → T p * S q = S q * T p\n\n  T_S_anticomm :\n    ∀ p, T p * S p = - (S p * T p)\n\nnamespace TiltSwitchSystem\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (TS : TiltSwitchSystem Op)\n\n/-- Tilt squares to one at each Cantor address slot. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem tilt_sq (p : ℕ) :\n    TS.T p * TS.T p = 1 :=\n  TS.T_sq p\n\n/-- Switch squares to one at each Cantor address slot. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem switch_sq (p : ℕ) :\n    TS.S p * TS.S p = 1 :=\n  TS.S_sq p\n\n/-- Tilt and switch anticommute at the same slot. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem tilt_switch_anticomm (p : ℕ) :\n    TS.T p * TS.S p + TS.S p * TS.T p = 0 := by\n  rw [TS.T_S_anticomm p]\n  simp\n\n/-- Tilt and switch commute at distinct slots. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem tilt_switch_comm_of_ne {p q : ℕ} (hpq : p ≠ q) :\n    TS.T p * TS.S q = TS.S q * TS.T p :=\n  TS.T_S_comm_ne p q hpq\n\nend TiltSwitchSystem\n\n/--\nReal doubled Hestenes/Krein Clifford representation generated from the\nCantor tilt/switch system.\n\n`gamma i` is the image of the `i`-th Clifford generator.  The paper-specific\nstring formula is retained as a witness field rather than reconstructed here.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  tiltSwitch : TiltSwitchSystem Op\n\n  gamma : ℕ → Op\n\n  gamma_sq :\n    ∀ i, gamma i * gamma i = 1\n\n  gamma_anticomm :\n    ∀ i j, i ≠ j → gamma i * gamma j = - (gamma j * gamma i)\n\n  stringFormulaWitness : Prop\n  stringFormulaWitness_holds : stringFormulaWitness\n\nnamespace RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (C : RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation Op)\n\n/-- Clifford square law readback. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_sq (i : ℕ) :\n    C.gamma i * C.gamma i = 1 :=\n  C.gamma_sq i\n\n/-- Clifford anticommutator readback. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_anticomm {i j : ℕ} (hij : i ≠ j) :\n    C.gamma i * C.gamma j + C.gamma j * C.gamma i = 0 := by\n  rw [C.gamma_anticomm i j hij]\n  simp\n\n/-- The concrete Cantor-address string formula is available as an owner witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem string_formula_holds :\n    C.stringFormulaWitness :=\n  C.stringFormulaWitness_holds\n\nend RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation\n\n/--\nInfinite-dimensional Cantor/Fock witness.\n\nThis packages the theorem-safe content: the real doubled Cantor function-space\nrepresentation generated by tilt/switch operators is calibrated to the Fock\nsocket.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure CelikKocakInfiniteFockWitness\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  cantorFunctionSpace : RealDoubledCantorFunctionSpace\n  tiltSwitch : TiltSwitchSystem Op\n  clifford : RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation Op\n  FockSpace : Type*\n  FockRepresentation : Type*\n  equivalentToFock : Prop\n  equivalentToFock_witness : equivalentToFock\n\nnamespace CelikKocakInfiniteFockWitness\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (W : CelikKocakInfiniteFockWitness Op)\n\n/-- The fractal Cantor representation is calibrated to the Fock socket. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem equivalent_to_fock :\n    W.equivalentToFock :=\n  W.equivalentToFock_witness\n\nend CelikKocakInfiniteFockWitness\n\n/--\nFinite-dimensional Cantor-Pauli witness over a real/doubled matrix carrier.\n\nThe representation on endpoint functions agrees with the real Pauli tensor lane\nthrough an explicit witness.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure FiniteCantorPauliWitness\n    (n : ℕ) (Mat : Type*) [Ring Mat] where\n  psiGamma : Fin (2 * n) → Mat\n\n  gamma_sq :\n    ∀ i, psiGamma i * psiGamma i = 1\n\n  gamma_anticomm :\n    ∀ i j, i ≠ j → psiGamma i * psiGamma j = - (psiGamma j * psiGamma i)\n\n  pauliTensorProductRealization : Prop\n  pauliTensorProductRealization_witness : pauliTensorProductRealization\n\nnamespace FiniteCantorPauliWitness\n\nvariable {n : ℕ} {Mat : Type*} [Ring Mat]\nvariable (W : FiniteCantorPauliWitness n Mat)\n\n/-- Finite Clifford square law readback. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_sq (i : Fin (2 * n)) :\n    W.psiGamma i * W.psiGamma i = 1 :=\n  W.gamma_sq i\n\n/-- Finite Clifford anticommutator readback. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem generator_anticomm {i j : Fin (2 * n)} (hij : i ≠ j) :\n    W.psiGamma i * W.psiGamma j + W.psiGamma j * W.psiGamma i = 0 := by\n  rw [W.gamma_anticomm i j hij]\n  simp\n\n/-- The endpoint representation is calibrated to the Pauli tensor-product lane. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem pauli_tensor_product_realization :\n    W.pauliTensorProductRealization :=\n  W.pauliTensorProductRealization_witness\n\nend FiniteCantorPauliWitness\n\n/--\nReal CAR pair.\n\nThis is the socket consumed by light-cone/Fock layers.  The construction from a\nchosen Clifford pair is witness-gated because the repo uses real doubled phase\nrather than scalar phase notation.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure RealCARPair\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  annihilation : Op\n  creation : Op\n\n  nilpotent_annihilation :\n    annihilation * annihilation = 0\n\n  nilpotent_creation :\n    creation * creation = 0\n\n  car :\n    annihilation * creation + creation * annihilation = 1\n\nnamespace RealCARPair\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (C : RealCARPair Op)\n\n/-- Annihilation is nilpotent. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem annihilation_sq_zero :\n    C.annihilation * C.annihilation = 0 :=\n  C.nilpotent_annihilation\n\n/-- Creation is nilpotent. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem creation_sq_zero :\n    C.creation * C.creation = 0 :=\n  C.nilpotent_creation\n\n/-- Canonical CAR anticommutator law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem anticommutator_eq_one :\n    C.annihilation * C.creation + C.creation * C.annihilation = 1 :=\n  C.car\n\nend RealCARPair\n\n/--\nClifford-to-CAR calibration.\n\nThis explicitly records that a selected Clifford pair from the Cantor\nrepresentation supplies the CAR pair required by the light-cone/Fock socket.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure CliffordToCARWitness\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  clifford : RealDoubledCantorCliffordRepresentation Op\n  gammaA : Op\n  gammaB : Op\n  carPair : RealCARPair Op\n\n  gammaA_is_generator :\n    ∃ i, gammaA = clifford.gamma i\n\n  gammaB_is_generator :\n    ∃ j, gammaB = clifford.gamma j\n\n  realDoubledPhaseCalibration : Prop\n  realDoubledPhaseCalibration_witness : realDoubledPhaseCalibration\n\nnamespace CliffordToCARWitness\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (W : CliffordToCARWitness Op)\n\n/-- The first selected CAR seed is a Clifford generator image. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem gammaA_generator :\n    ∃ i, W.gammaA = W.clifford.gamma i :=\n  W.gammaA_is_generator\n\n/-- The second selected CAR seed is a Clifford generator image. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem gammaB_generator :\n    ∃ j, W.gammaB = W.clifford.gamma j :=\n  W.gammaB_is_generator\n\n/-- The Clifford-to-CAR construction uses the real doubled phase calibration. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem real_doubled_phase_calibrated :\n    W.realDoubledPhaseCalibration :=\n  W.realDoubledPhaseCalibration_witness\n\nend CliffordToCARWitness\n\n/--\nCalibration between repository Drazin/chiral arrows and the Cantor tilt/switch\nwitness.\n\nThis prevents identifying tilt/switch operators with `u_+`, `u_-`, or mirror\noperators without an explicit representation map.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure DrazinArrowTiltSwitchCalibration\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  tiltSwitch : TiltSwitchSystem Op\n\n  uPlus : Op\n  uMinus : Op\n  mirror : Op\n\n  uPlus_realized :\n    ∃ p, uPlus = tiltSwitch.T p\n\n  uMinus_realized :\n    ∃ p, uMinus = tiltSwitch.T p ∨ uMinus = tiltSwitch.S p\n\n  mirror_realized_by_switch :\n    ∃ p, mirror = tiltSwitch.S p\n\nnamespace DrazinArrowTiltSwitchCalibration\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (C : DrazinArrowTiltSwitchCalibration Op)\n\n/-- Positive light-cone arrow is calibrated to a tilt/switch witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem uPlus_calibrated :\n    ∃ p, C.uPlus = C.tiltSwitch.T p :=\n  C.uPlus_realized\n\n/-- Negative light-cone arrow is calibrated to a tilt/switch witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem uMinus_calibrated :\n    ∃ p, C.uMinus = C.tiltSwitch.T p ∨ C.uMinus = C.tiltSwitch.S p :=\n  C.uMinus_realized\n\n/-- Mirror data is calibrated to a switch witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem mirror_calibrated :\n    ∃ p, C.mirror = C.tiltSwitch.S p :=\n  C.mirror_realized_by_switch\n\nend DrazinArrowTiltSwitchCalibration\n\n/--\nFractal Cantor Fock witness packet.\n\nThis is the topology-side object closing the boundary-to-Fock socket:\nCantor boundary, tilt/switch Clifford representation, CAR/Fock witness, and\ncalibrated Drazin/chiral arrows.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure FractalCantorFockWitness\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  celikKocak : CelikKocakInfiniteFockWitness Op\n  cliffordToCAR : CliffordToCARWitness Op\n  drazinCalibration : DrazinArrowTiltSwitchCalibration Op\n  fockSocketClosed : Prop\n  fockSocketClosed_witness : fockSocketClosed\n\nnamespace FractalCantorFockWitness\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\nvariable (W : FractalCantorFockWitness Op)\n\n/-- The Cantor/Fock witness closes the light-cone Fock socket, as supplied. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem closes_fock_socket :\n    W.fockSocketClosed :=\n  W.fockSocketClosed_witness\n\n/-- Re-export of the Fock equivalence witness. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem equivalent_to_fock :\n    W.celikKocak.equivalentToFock :=\n  W.celikKocak.equivalentToFock_witness\n\n/-- Re-export of the real doubled Clifford-to-CAR calibration. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem real_doubled_phase_calibrated :\n    W.cliffordToCAR.realDoubledPhaseCalibration :=\n  W.cliffordToCAR.realDoubledPhaseCalibration_witness\n\nend FractalCantorFockWitness\n\n/-- Drazin support of a signal operator: `p = A Aᴰ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure DrazinHorizon\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  A : Op\n  AD : Op\n  p : Op\n\n  p_def :\n    p = A * AD\n\n  commute :\n    A * AD = AD * A\n\n  p_idempotent :\n    p * p = p\n\n/-- Drazin-Green harmonic projector: `H = 1 - L Lᴰ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure DrazinGreenHarmonic\n    (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] where\n  L : Op\n  LD : Op\n  H : Op\n\n  H_def :\n    H = 1 - L * LD\n\n  H_idempotent :\n    H * H = H\n\n/-- Matter envelope extracted from the Cantor/Fock observable. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef fractalFockMatterEnvelope\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (D : DrazinHorizon Op)\n    (G : DrazinGreenHarmonic Op)\n    (x : Op) : Op :=\n  G.H * (D.p * x * D.p) * G.H\n\n/-- Real Fierz readout channels.  The phase-like channel is named `rotor`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ninductive FierzChannel where\n  | scalar\n  | rotor\n  | vector\n  | axial\n  | area\n  deriving DecidableEq, Fintype\n\n/-- Real Fierz readout packet. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure FierzReadout\n    (Op : Type*) where\n  channel : FierzChannel → Op → ℝ\n\n/--\nFierz coordinates are read from the Drazin-Hodge envelope, not from the raw\nCantor/Fock operator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef fractalFockFierzCoordinate\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (D : DrazinHorizon Op)\n    (G : DrazinGreenHarmonic Op)\n    (R : FierzReadout Op)\n    (x : Op)\n    (ch : FierzChannel) : ℝ :=\n  R.channel ch (fractalFockMatterEnvelope D G x)\n\n/--\nMetric graph compression for finite endpoint geometries.\n\nThis is deliberately separate from the Clifford/Fock witness lane.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nstructure FiniteEndpointMetricGraphCompression\n    (n : ℕ) where\n  Endpoint : Type*\n  MetricData : Type*\n  WeightedGraph : Type*\n  embedding : Endpoint → WeightedGraph\n  endpointAddress : Endpoint → CantorAddress n\n  optimalityOrCompressionWitness : Prop\n  optimalityOrCompressionWitness_holds : optimalityOrCompressionWitness\n\nnamespace FiniteEndpointMetricGraphCompression\n\nvariable {n : ℕ}\nvariable (G : FiniteEndpointMetricGraphCompression n)\n\n/-- The finite graph layer is a metric compression witness, not a Clifford witness. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem compression_witness_holds :\n    G.optimalityOrCompressionWitness :=\n  G.optimalityOrCompressionWitness_holds\n\nend FiniteEndpointMetricGraphCompression\n\nend InfoGeometry.Topology.FractalCantorFockWitness\n","mtime":1778782701648}